<title>PERU: Peru stops rice imports from disease-hit nations.</title>
<headline>Peru stops rice imports from disease-hit nations.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Peruvian government suspended Wednesday rice imports from countries affected by the Gorgojo Khapra disease, government officials confirmed.</p>
<p>An Agriculture Ministry decree said the measure was necessary to prevent &quot;increasing the risk of entry of the disease, which would cause grave damage to the national agriculture.&quot;</p>
<p>U.S. rice sources said the suspension of phyto-sanitary certificiates for those rice imports would affect all origins except the United States, Thailand, Argentina and Ecuador which are unaffected by the Khapra beetle.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
